        "title": "New ‘Steve Jobs in Exile’ book reads like a lost season of your favorite series",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/20/new-steve-jobs-in-exile-book-reads-like-a-lost-season-of-your-favorite-series/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/02/steve-jobs-exile.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>This week marked the release of ‘Steve Jobs in Exile: The Untold Story of NeXT and the Remaking of an American Visionary,’ by author Geoffrey Cain, a deliciously thorough book that dives deep into the years that most people overlook when retelling the Apple co-founder’s famous redemption story.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"steve-jobs\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1052801\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/20/new-steve-jobs-in-exile-book-reads-like-a-lost-season-of-your-favorite-series/#more-1052801\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
