        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/15/iphone-vibe-coding-app-ships-first-update-in-four-months-after-app-store-review-issue/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/replit.webp?w=1600\" /></div><p>All’s well that ends well in App Store review controversies. Back in March, a major agentic coding company made news when Apple reportedly pushed back on new versions of its iPhone app.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Two months later, the head of the company says they “worked things out with Apple,” and they have a big new app update to show for it.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"ai,app-store,apps,replit\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1052372\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/15/iphone-vibe-coding-app-ships-first-update-in-four-months-after-app-store-review-issue/#more-1052372\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
