        "content_text": "<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/may/20/uk-radio-station-apologises-for-accidentally-announcing-kings-death\">Guardian</a>: \"Due to a computer error at our main studio, the Death of a Monarch procedure, which all UK stations hold in readiness while hoping not to require, was accidentally activated on Tuesday afternoon (19 May), mistakenly announcing that HM the King had passed away.\" <a href=\"https://www.euronews.com/my-europe/2026/05/20/former-uk-pirate-radio-station-sorry-after-mistakenly-announcing-death-of-king-charles\">Euronews</a>: \"Caroline has been pleased to broadcast Her Majesty the Queen's and now the King's, Christmas message and we hope to do so for many years to come,\" he said, referring to the monarch's traditional Christmas Day message to the nation. \"We apologise to HM (his majesty) the king and to our listeners for any distress caused,\" Moore added.",
