        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/Apple-Sports-world-cup-update.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>Apple’s Sports app was just updated to version 4.0, adding new features for the upcoming World Cup and expanding the app’s availability worldwide. Here’s what’s new.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apple-sports\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1052730\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/19/apple-sports-app-launches-world-cup-support-in-new-update/#more-1052730\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
